---
layout: changelog
title: "Run PostgreSQL 19 and upgrade to it online from the Console"
date: 2026-11-27
cover: /images/blog/announcing-postgresql-19/cover.avif
tags: databases, console
---

Appwrite [managed PostgreSQL databases](/docs/products/databases/postgresql#versions) now support PostgreSQL 19, released by the PostgreSQL project on November 19. New databases run PostgreSQL 19 by default, and PostgreSQL 18 and 17 remain supported.

Existing databases upgrade online from a new **Version** card under **Settings** > **General**, or with `createUpgrade` through the API. Reads continue during the upgrade, and writes pause only at the cutover, when open connections are closed and your application reconnects. An upgrade can't be reversed, so check the [PostgreSQL 19 behavior changes](/docs/products/databases/postgresql/maintenance#postgresql-19) and your extensions before you start.

